From afdfa497b66a0867304a5e74282da8122420a470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 18:10:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 435/572] fix(st): check return values of NVMEM functions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fix a few issues reported by Coverity in the STM32 NVMEM helpers.

In stm32_get_otp_value_from_idx(), drop the useless initialization of
"ret" to BSEC_NOT_SUPPORTED, which was reported as a dead assignment.

In stm32_save_boot_info(), properly check and propagate the return
values of nvmem_cell_read() and nvmem_cell_write() instead of ignoring
them. This avoids unchecked-return-value reports from Coverity.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 1d65b5f6a2aaab777ba92b6ee3a86d2a24d05ee7 fix(st): check return values of NVMEM functions]
Change-Id: Ia156f99714f5465ff3415aef333c354a2bafe8bd
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/546321
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c b/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c
index 132a8fa029..640bfd7755 100644
--- a/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c
+++ b/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ int stm32_get_otp_value(const char *otp_name, uint32_t *otp_val)
 
 int stm32_get_otp_value_from_idx(const uint32_t otp_idx, uint32_t *otp_val)
 {
-	uint32_t ret = BSEC_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+	uint32_t ret;
 
 	assert(otp_val != NULL);
 
@@ -487,10 +487,16 @@ int stm32_save_boot_info(boot_api_context_t *boot_context)
 	if (ret != 0) {
 		return ret;
 	}
-	nvmem_cell_read(&boot_mode, (uint8_t *)&reg_val, sizeof(reg_val), NULL);
+	ret = nvmem_cell_read(&boot_mode, (uint8_t *)&reg_val, sizeof(reg_val), NULL);
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		return ret;
+	}
 	reg_val &= ~clear;
 	reg_val |= set;
-	nvmem_cell_write(&boot_mode, (uint8_t *)&reg_val, sizeof(reg_val));
+	ret = nvmem_cell_write(&boot_mode, (uint8_t *)&reg_val, sizeof(reg_val));
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
